    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "No strategic_frame.json exists for this deck; names were read against CONTEXT.md (Selesnya blink plus counters, Emiel as the engine) and every cluster's card list. No cluster has a verified_count, because the deck has no passing stack yet.",
      "Veldt sits in city-3-hood-0 among counters spells. It is a land and belongs with city-0; CardBERT likely read the counters it stores. It looks misplaced, not unusual.",
      "city-4 groups by theme (flying creatures) more than by job. Restoration Angel, Karmic Guide, Nurturing Pixie and Sun Titan share the rebuy/blink job; Hanged Executioner fits loosely; Gilded Goose is the odd member, a mana creature pulled in by being a flyer, and its 'Ramp' fallback comes from that one card.",
      "city-5 reads clean as multipliers (Doubling Season, Hardened Scales, Branching Evolution, Pir, Panharmonicon, Seedborn Muse). Archaeomancer's Map is the odd member: land ramp and catch-up, not a doubler.",
      "city-4 and city-5 each have a single neighbourhood identical to the city, so those neighbourhoods are left unnamed and the renderer falls back.",
      "city-1 and city-2 split partly by colour and supertype (green value creatures vs white counters creatures, with the legends grouped together), as you would expect from the CardBERT space. The split between them is real but is not purely a split by job: many cards on both sides put counters on things when they enter.",
      "city-0-hood-2 (Forest, Plains, Savannah) is grouped by basic land types. Savannah fits there because it has both types, and the split reads clean."
    ]
  },
